WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.795 --> 00:00:20.637
My memories of the next three days and nights are very dim, but I know that Diana and

2
00:00:20.677 --> 00:00:23.538
Mary appeared at my bedside once or twice a day.

3
00:00:23.558 --> 00:00:27.939
"It's good we took her in," whispered Mary during one visit.

4
00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:32.060
"She certainly would have died if she stayed outside all night.

5
00:00:33.256 --> 00:00:34.717
I wonder what she has suffered."

6
00:00:35.878 --> 00:00:38.659
"Strange hardships, I imagine," said Diana.

7
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:45.263
"She seems like an educated person from her manner of speaking, and her clothes are fine and barely

8
00:00:45.303 --> 00:00:52.987
worn." On the afternoon of the fourth day, I struggled from bed, washed and dressed myself with difficulty,

9
00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:56.689
and went down to the kitchen, where Hannah was busy baking.

10
00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:02.172
The young ladies and their brother had gone for a walk, but would soon be back for tea.

11
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:09.302
As I watched Hannah make a pie, she told me about the Rivers family and their home, which

12
00:01:09.362 --> 00:01:10.762
was known as Moor House.

13
00:01:12.803 --> 00:01:18.404
St. John Rivers was a minister at a church a few miles away in Morton, the very place

14
00:01:18.424 --> 00:01:20.885
where I'd tried to trade my things for a roll.

15
00:01:22.065 --> 00:01:28.107
His sisters worked as governesses in a distant city and had come home for their father's recent funeral.

16
00:01:28.127 --> 00:01:29.787
"You're up!"

17
00:01:30.227 --> 00:01:32.468
cried Mary when the three siblings returned.

18
00:01:33.568 --> 00:01:36.130
"You still look so pale and thin, poor girl."

19
00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.592
"What are you doing in the kitchen?"

20
00:01:38.973 --> 00:01:39.693
asked Diana.

21
00:01:39.713 --> 00:01:45.258
"Mary and I like to sit here, but you're a visitor and must go into the parlor."

22
00:01:46.399 --> 00:01:50.663
She assisted me into the parlor, where I sat on a sofa to wait for tea.

23
00:01:51.924 --> 00:01:56.928
St. John sat opposite me, silently reading, so I used the time to study him.

24
00:01:58.209 --> 00:02:04.089
He was in his late twenties, tall and slender, with a classically handsome face and fair hair.

25
00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.851
When tea was placed on the table, St.

26
00:02:07.871 --> 00:02:13.073
John addressed me for the first time, urging me to eat slowly so as not to make myself

27
00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:18.815
ill. "I hope I won't be eating long at your expense, sir," I replied.

28
00:02:18.835 --> 00:02:21.496
"No," he said coolly.

29
00:02:21.516 --> 00:02:25.958
"When you've given us the address of your friends, we'll see that you're returned home."

30
00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:29.620
"I must tell you that I have no family or friends."

31
00:02:30.928 --> 00:02:36.032
All three looked at me, but I felt no suspicion in their eyes, only curiosity.

32
00:02:36.052 --> 00:02:38.313
"You've never been married?"

33
00:02:39.454 --> 00:02:42.356
St. John glanced at my hands, looking for a wedding ring.

34
00:02:43.637 --> 00:02:44.518
Diana laughed.

35
00:02:44.538 --> 00:02:48.601
"She can't be more than 17 or 18 years old, St.

36
00:02:48.621 --> 00:02:52.924
John." "I'm almost 19, and no, I'm not married."

37
00:02:54.165 --> 00:02:58.388
I felt my face grow hot as bitter memories were awakened by the mention of marriage.

38
00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.463
They all saw the embarrassment and the emotion in my face.

39
00:03:04.344 --> 00:03:10.589
Diana and Mary looked away, but their colder and sterner brother continued to stare until tears filled my

40
00:03:10.749 --> 00:03:13.151
eyes. "Where did you last live?"

41
00:03:13.532 --> 00:03:14.092
he asked.

42
00:03:14.112 --> 00:03:16.794
"You are too inquisitive, St.

43
00:03:16.814 --> 00:03:22.719
John," murmured Mary, but he leaned over the table and required an answer with a second firm and

44
00:03:22.799 --> 00:03:23.580
piercing look.

45
00:03:24.741 --> 00:03:28.444
"Where I lived and with whom are my secrets," I replied concisely.

46
00:03:29.588 --> 00:03:32.809
"And, in my opinion, you have the right to keep those secrets from St.

47
00:03:32.829 --> 00:03:35.770
John and every other questioner," said Diana.

48
00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:39.971
"But if I know nothing about you, I can't help you," St.

49
00:03:39.991 --> 00:03:40.751
John said to me.

50
00:03:40.771 --> 00:03:43.212
"And you need help, don't you?"

51
00:03:43.232 --> 00:03:44.653
"I do."

52
00:03:45.733 --> 00:03:48.154
I had now drunk my tea and was quite refreshed.

53
00:03:48.174 --> 00:03:53.355
"I will tell you as much of my story as I can without compromising my own peace of

54
00:03:53.435 --> 00:03:55.736
mind and security and that of others."

55
00:03:57.652 --> 00:04:03.596
And so I told them that I was an orphan, educated at Lowood, and that until recently I

56
00:04:03.656 --> 00:04:04.397
was a governess.

57
00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:10.241
It was too dangerous to explain the reason for my departure, but I was blameless.

58
00:04:10.261 --> 00:04:13.103
"Don't make her talk anymore now, St.

59
00:04:13.123 --> 00:04:15.204
John," said Diana when I paused.

60
00:04:16.305 --> 00:04:17.546
"Miss Elliott is tired."

61
00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:21.269
I startled at the sound of that name, and St.

62
00:04:21.289 --> 00:04:22.329
John noticed at once.

63
00:04:22.349 --> 00:04:27.024
"You did say your name was Jane Elliott?"

64
00:04:27.044 --> 00:04:30.666
"Yes, I have taken an alias because I fear discovery above all else.

65
00:04:31.867 --> 00:04:34.048
I do not want to be dependent on you for long.

66
00:04:35.269 --> 00:04:39.831
Show me how to seek work, then let me go, but until then, allow me to stay here."

67
00:04:39.851 --> 00:04:43.913
"Indeed you shall stay here," Diana said firmly.

68
00:04:43.933 --> 00:04:47.195
"You shall," repeated Mary.

69
00:04:47.215 --> 00:04:51.778
"I will be a dressmaker or a servant," I vowed.

70
00:04:51.798 --> 00:04:54.759
"If such is your spirit," St.

71
00:04:54.779 --> 00:04:58.906
John said without emotion, "I promise to aid you in my own time and way."

72
00:05:00.027 --> 00:05:02.709
He then resumed his reading, and I soon went to bed.

73
00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:09.173
As the days passed, I found that the more I knew Diana and Mary, the more I liked

74
00:05:09.233 --> 00:05:14.838
them. They were better educated than I was, and Diana offered to teach me German.

75
00:05:16.038 --> 00:05:19.981
When they discovered I could draw, they gave me their pencils and watercolors.

76
00:05:21.202 --> 00:05:23.752
I did not feel such a connection to St.

77
00:05:23.772 --> 00:05:27.735
John, but that may have been because he was often away, tending to his parishioners.

78
00:05:28.996 --> 00:05:31.538
He also had a reserved, brooding nature.

79
00:05:32.678 --> 00:05:37.142
A month sped by, and Diana and Mary were soon to leave Moor House.

80
00:05:39.063 --> 00:05:43.886
St. John was going back to the parsonage, but he'd said nothing to me about the employment he

81
00:05:43.926 --> 00:05:47.149
had promised, so one morning I ventured to inquire.

82
00:05:47.169 --> 00:05:51.412
"Two years ago Morton had no school," he replied.

83
00:05:52.564 --> 00:05:55.627
"I started one for boys, and now I'm opening one for girls.

84
00:05:56.808 --> 00:06:00.451
I fear the work is beneath you, but would you be the schoolmistress?"

85
00:06:00.471 --> 00:06:02.373
"Thank you, Mr.

86
00:06:02.393 --> 00:06:03.854
Rivers," I said quickly.

87
00:06:03.874 --> 00:06:06.036
"I accept your offer."

88
00:06:06.056 --> 00:06:09.359
"You do understand that it's only a village school?

89
00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:14.604
Knitting, sewing, reading, writing, and mathematics will be all you'll teach."

90
00:06:15.865 --> 00:06:19.148
I understood and told him I was still happy to accept the position.

91
00:06:20.332 --> 00:06:24.994
Diana and Mary became sadder and more silent as the day approached for their departure.

92
00:06:26.835 --> 00:06:28.836
They hinted that they might never see St.

93
00:06:28.856 --> 00:06:31.697
John again because he intended to become a missionary.

94
00:06:32.918 --> 00:06:37.760
Adding to their gloom was a newly arrived letter announcing that their uncle John had died.

95
00:06:39.081 --> 00:06:45.544
Years before, John had given their father some bad financial advice that had ruined the elder Mr.

96
00:06:45.584 --> 00:06:51.557
Rivers. They had always hoped that John would atone for this by leaving them his estate, but the

97
00:06:51.617 --> 00:06:55.839
letter said that he had bequeathed twenty thousand pounds to another relative.

98
00:06:57.079 --> 00:06:59.560
The next day I left Moor House for Morton.

99
00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:04.241
Diana and Mary soon returned home, and with St.

100
00:07:04.261 --> 00:07:08.242
John and Hannah leaving a week later, the old house was abandoned.

101
00:07:09.543 --> 00:07:16.718
My new home was a cottage, furnished simply by Rosamond Oliver, the only daughter of the richest man

102
00:07:16.778 --> 00:07:17.359
in the valley.
